{% if data_science_layout %}
This project also carries the data-science layer, so two trees coexist:

- `app/` — the FastAPI service (routers, schemas, models, settings).
  Keep request/response handling here; do not put analysis code in it.
- `src/` — the analysis pipeline (`data/`, `features/`, `models/`,
  `visualization/`), plus `notebooks/` and `reports/` for exploration
  artifacts. Data, model and report outputs stay out of git.

The intended split: heavy processing lives in `src/` scripts/notebooks and
writes its results where the service can read them; `app/` routers expose
those results over HTTP. If a router needs a `src/` helper directly, move
the helper into an importable module and add its dependencies to
`[project] dependencies` first (the stubs are linted like any other `src/`
code, so `deptry` flags undeclared imports there too).
